{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.74,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U7", "U31"],
      "pins": ["U7.4", "U7.5", "U31.4", "U31.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both isolated CAN transceivers have their logic-side and bus-side ground pins tied to the same board GND net: U7 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2), and U31 pin 4 (GND1) and pin 5 (GND2), are all connected to net GND.",
      "expected": "The specification states the board implements two isolated CAN buses through isolated CAN transceivers. For galvanic isolation, GND1 (logic side) and GND2 (CAN bus side) must be separate ground nets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ...) (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ...) ... (node (ref \"U31\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\") ...) (node (ref \"U31\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The isolation barrier is shorted; CAN0 and CAN1 are not galvanically isolated as intended, enabling ground loops and defeating the specified isolated motor/actuator interface.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["D16", "R8"],
      "pins": ["D16.2", "D16.4", "R8.1", "R8.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0196", "Net-(D16-K2)"],
      "observed": "D16 pin 4 (A2) is on NET0196, and D16 pin 2 (K2) is connected through R8 back to the same NET0196 node. This places R8 directly across the LED terminals with no return path to a supply or ground.",
      "expected": "An LED indicator should have one terminal connected to a driven signal and the other terminal connected through a current-limiting resistor to a fixed rail or ground, providing a complete current path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"138\") (name \"NET0196\") ... (node (ref \"D16\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"A2\") ...) (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"158\") (name \"Net-(D16-K2)\") ... (node (ref \"D16\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"K2\") ...) (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"1\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The second LED section of D16 cannot light; any intended e-stop/status indication from that LED is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.58
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R48"],
      "pins": ["R48.1", "R48.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R48 is given the schematic value \"24k\", but its MPN and description specify a 24Ω part: MPN \"FRC0805J240TSD\" and description \"... 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor ...\".",
      "expected": "The value field, MPN, and description should agree. A 24Ω 0805 125mW resistor across VOUTP/VOUTN is inconsistent with the 24k value used in the schematic/SPICE and would be an order-of-magnitude error if sourced from the MPN.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R48\") (value \"24k\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") (value \"FRC0805J240TSD\")) ... (field (name \"Description\") (value \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R48 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If assembled using the MPN/description, a 24Ω resistor would heavily load and potentially overheat the VOUTP/VOUTN node; if assembled using the schematic value, the BOM metadata is inconsistent and could lead to a sourcing mistake.",
      "confidence": 0.61
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The strongest anomaly is that the specified isolated CAN transceivers have GND1 and GND2 tied together, defeating CAN isolation. The files also show a dual-LED current-limiting resistor connected across the LED terminals and an R48 value/MPN mismatch."
}

